--
-- The canonical fixture vector must pass BOTH the structural check and
-- the semantic replay. The four mutant vectors below were produced by
-- the generating harness from structurally VALID bundles (Rust
-- `encode_bundle_v1`, which folds in the structural validator, accepts
-- every one): a transparent-delta step whose target is not the
-- signature body, a beta step whose target is not the instantiated
-- body, a variable-lookup certificate whose inferred type is not the
-- context lookup, and an application certificate whose recorded
-- dependent result is the raw instantiation rather than its kernel
-- normal form (the bounded-normalization reconciliation). Each decodes
-- and passes the structural check, and each fails the semantic replay
-- — the discriminating evidence that Phase E checks what the
-- structural layer cannot. Development regression vectors, not
-- correspondence authority.

